===Glyph origin===
{{Han etym}}
Possibly a {{Han compound|爻|六|c1=p|c2=p|ls=psc|nocap=y}}. Later, {{och-l|*𦥑}} was added to form {{och-l|*𦥯}}, and a semantic {{och-l|*子|child}} was added for differentiation.

Another explanation is {{Han compound|敎|𦥑|宀|t1=to teach|t2=mingling hands; hands-on learning|t3=house; roofed building|abb1=y}} – a child learning in a roofed place. However, the oracle bone script does not include a child.

In the modern form, 六 has corrupted to {{l-lite|zh|sc=Hani|冖|t=cover}}, and the hands 𦥑 around the {{l-lite|zh|sc=Hani|爻}} have become connected with the 冖. ''{{w|Shuowen}}'' regards {{och-l|𦥑}} as the phonetic component in the character, which may be true according to some Old Chinese reconstructions such as that of {{w|Pan Wuyun}}'s, though probably not others.

See also the top component of [[覺]], which is a contraction of 學.

===Etymology 1===
{{zh-forms|s=学|alt=斈,𢻯,𡕕,𣁃,𫝯,𭓕,𭓘}}
Endopassive/volitional derivation of {{och-l|覺|to become aware|id=2}} ({{zh-ref|Sagart, 2004}}; {{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}; {{zh-ref|Baxter and Sagart, 2014}}). Ultimately from {{inh-lite|zh|sit-pro|*kruk||to [[rouse]]; to [[awaken]]; to [[disturb]]}}.

