===Glyph origin===
{{Han etym}}
Oracle bone script: {{Han compound|宀|𢑓|c1=s|c2=p|t1=roof|t2=male pig|ls=psc}}.<ref name="殷墟甲骨文“■”、“■”兩字考辨">姚萱，2016, 殷墟甲骨文“■”、“■”兩字考辨 in《中国文字研究》，上海：上海书店出版社，2016年8月第二十三辑。</ref> An archaic variant closer to the original drawing is [[𡩀]]. See {{zh-l|𢑓}} for more. Similar to [[冡]].

Later the phonetic component have been corrupted to 豕, so {{w|Shuowen Jiezi}} erroneously analyzed it as {{Han compound|宀|豭|abb2=y|c1=s|c2=p|t1=roof|t2=pig|ls=psc}}.

All etymologies based on the modern version of the phonetic component (豕) are folk etymologies since they miss the original component (𢑓).
<references/>

